# The build context is the repo root, and the repo root is ~52GB — target/
# alone is 50 of it. Without this the daemon receives all of it before the
# first line of the Dockerfile runs.
#
# Named for the Dockerfile rather than placed at the repo root so it applies to
# this build only: Dockerfile and Dockerfile.rendezvous take the same root as
# their context and must NOT inherit an allowlist that excludes the source.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit exactly what the Dockerfile reads. The source
# tree arrives at runtime over the bind mount, never through the image.
*
# A glob, not the two names: adding a third script and forgetting this line
# fails the build with a "not found" that points at the Dockerfile, not here.
!.devcontainer/*.sh
